1:["$","$Le",null,{"guide":{"slug":"help-new-plants-settle","number":"03","category":"PLANT CARE","title":"Helping new plants settle in","intro":"Good preparation and steady observation make it easier to understand how your new plants are adjusting. Start with the instructions for the plants you bought.","image":"/mas-aquarium-studio/plants.jpg","alt":"Anubias leaves held above an aquarium at Micro Aquatic Shop","takeaway":"Use the right planting method and watch new growth before changing the routine.","sections":[{"id":"prepare","title":"Prepare before planting","body":"Have your tools ready and keep the plants damp while you work. Remove the packaging and growing material as appropriate for the product. Tissue-culture plants and potted plants need different preparation."},{"id":"position","title":"Plant according to the type","body":"Keep the rhizomes of Anubias and Java fern exposed. Follow the planting method for rooted and stem plants. Place floating plants on the surface and consider the shade they cast below."},{"id":"observe","title":"Look for what is changing","body":"Observe new growth and remove dead or decaying plant material. Record when changes begin. Photos taken from the same angle can help you discuss a concern with the shop."},{"id":"routine","title":"Keep a consistent routine","body":"Use a lighting timer and a routine suited to your aquarium. Check that the filter and temperature equipment work. Follow fertiliser instructions for the product and setup; ask for advice before making several changes together."}],"questions":["Have I prepared this plant correctly?","Which part should stay above the substrate?","What information should I bring if it is struggling?"],"sources":[{"title":"Tropica — Planting","url":"https://tropica.com/en/guide/get-the-right-start/planting/"},{"title":"Tropica — Growing in","url":"https://tropica.com/en/guide/get-the-right-start/growing-in/"},{"title":"Tropica — Plant care FAQ","url":"https://tropica.com/en/guide/faq/"}],"next":"choose-plants","shopPlants":true}}]
